{
  "raw": {
    "https://laroche.edu/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/13927-Career-Out-Infograph.pdf": {
      "title": "13927",
      "description": "13927\nCAREER  OUTCOMES  | CLASS OF 2024\nOFFICE OF CAREER AND PROFESSIONAL DEVELOPMENT\nCLASS OF 2024\nINTRODUCTION\nhe La Roche University Class of 2024 consists of students  \nwho graduated in August 2023, December 2023, and May 2024. \nThe First Destination Survey was initiated by the Office of Career and \nProfessional Development prior to graduation and concluded approximately \none year after each graduation date. \nAdditional data was gathered from online sources, employers and faculty .  \nThis method of reporting career outcomes data follows the reporting guidelines \nestablished by the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE). \nLa Roche made a good faith effort to verify the information obtained by all \nsources other than the responding graduates.\nT\nOUTCOMES \nTERMINOLOGY\nCohort Size: Number of students.  \nCareer Outcomes: The percentage  \nof graduates who are employed full- or \npart-time, in military or volunteer service, \nand/or enrolled in continuing education.\nKnowledge Rate: The percentage of \ngraduates for which the institution has \nreasonable and verifiable information \nconcerning the graduates’ post-graduation \ncareer activities.\n 185 - COHORT SIZE\n 72 % - KNOWLEDGE RATE\n 97 % - CAREER OUTCOMES\nBACHELOR’S\nLA ROCHE UNIVERSITY   |   9000 BABCOCK BOULEVARD   |   PITTSBURGH, PA 15237   |   laroche.edu\nAUGUST 2023, DECEMBER 2023 AND MAY 2024\n 6 - COHORT SIZE \n 50 % - KNOWLEDGE RATE\n 100 % - CAREER OUTCOMES\nASSOCIATE\n 171 - COHORT SIZE \n 49 % - KNOWLEDGE RATE\n 95 % - CAREER OUTCOMES\nMASTER’S\n 362 - COHORT SIZE \n 63 % - KNOWLEDGE RATE\n 97 % - CAREER OUTCOMES\nALL DEGREES\nDATA COLLECTION \nMETHODS\nData was collected for all graduates \nwho obtained a degree from La Roche \nUniversity during the designated \nacademic year. The following steps \nwere followed during the data \ncollection period:\n1 Shortly before graduation, potential  \n graduates were identified by the  \n La Roche University Registrar and  \n Office of Career and Professional  \n Development. These students were  \n sent emails inviting them to complete  \n the First Destination Survey . \n2 The list of survey respondents  \n was continuously updated for  \n accuracy after graduation based on  \n a student’s degree status.\n3 Over a 0ne-year period, automated  \n reminder emails were sent out from \n the Handshake platform to graduates  \n who had yet to respond.\n4 Data provided by the August 2023, \n December 2023 and May 2024 \n cohorts were combined to produce  \n this annual report.\n5 Outcomes data were presented by  \n degree for the entire graduating class  \n year and also by degree type. "
    },
